WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.909 --> 00:00:05.021
The heroes of The Walking Dead are what drew
the majority of viewers to the show, but the

00:00:05.021 --> 00:00:09.500
villainous Negan, as played by Jeffrey Dean
Morgan, quickly developed into one of the

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:12.475
most complex characters in the series.  Here's how.

00:00:13.214 --> 00:00:17.734
Walking Dead viewers first meet Negan in the
season 6 finale, "Last Day On Earth," and

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:19.810
he makes a big first impression.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:24.470
Not only do he and his faction known as the
Saviors capture Rick and his allies, but Negan

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:28.748
gleefully murders both Abraham and Glenn in
a pretty brutal manner.

00:00:28.748 --> 00:00:34.050
He comes off as cold, conniving, and unspeakably
violent, leaving viewers to wonder, where

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.320
could someone so remorseless have come from?

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.780
Before leading the Saviors and swinging his
barbed-wire baseball bat around, Negan was

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.000
a pretty average guy.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.619
As a kid in Virginia, he quickly gained a
reputation as a bully and troublemaker, but

00:00:46.619 --> 00:00:50.930
that changed when he eventually met a woman
Lucille, portrayed on The Walking Dead by

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:53.734
Morgan's real-life spouse, Hilarie Burton-Morgan.

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:58.329
The two fell in love, married and hoped to
start a family, only for their situation to

00:00:58.329 --> 00:00:59.334
quickly sour.

00:00:59.334 --> 00:01:04.199
Losing his job as a gym teacher after a fight
at a local bar, Negan retreated into video

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:05.363
games for a while.

00:01:05.363 --> 00:01:07.278
"Are you playing with children?"

00:01:07.278 --> 00:01:08.807
"Uhhh… teenagers.

00:01:08.807 --> 00:01:09.735
I think.

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:10.735
Mostly."

00:01:10.735 --> 00:01:15.520
And at one point, he cheated on Lucille, and
to make matters worse, Lucille was diagnosed

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:19.084
with pancreatic cancer shortly before the
apocalypse began.

00:01:19.084 --> 00:01:23.605
Negan does his best to provide her with medicine
in their now walker-infested world, but she

00:01:23.605 --> 00:01:25.900
ultimately dies from her illness.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:30.897
This drives Negan over the edge and he begins
tapping into his darker, more cynical side.

00:01:30.897 --> 00:01:35.420
Sometime later, the Saviors form with him
as their leader, making him and Lucille — his

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:38.871
barbed wire baseball bat - a symbol of fear.

00:01:38.871 --> 00:01:43.501
Negan has remained a constant presence on
The Walking Dead since his debut, arguably

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:46.129
becoming the most interesting part of the
program.

00:01:46.129 --> 00:01:52.020
He even got his own flashback episode in season
10, aptly titled "Here's Negan," further exploring

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.636
his life, pre-apocalypse.

00:01:53.636 --> 00:01:57.840
Of the series' main antagonists, Negan has
secured the most appearances, popping up in

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.560
over 40 episodes across three and a half seasons.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:04.910
In addition, he has the longest lifespan of
the bunch, sticking around the land of the

00:02:04.910 --> 00:02:07.034
living for roughly 60 installments.

00:02:07.034 --> 00:02:12.100
His interactions with Alpha make him the first
bad guy to meet their successor, and him subsequently

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:15.884
killing her makes him the only main villain
to defeat another villain.

00:02:15.884 --> 00:02:20.700
Perhaps most importantly, Negan is the sole
antagonist to turn a new leaf and become something

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:21.535
of a good guy.

00:02:21.535 --> 00:02:26.250
Also worth mentioning is that Negan boasts
the highest kill count so far, with roughly

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:29.006
230 deaths credited to his actions.

00:02:29.006 --> 00:02:31.870
Included in those deaths are six main cast
members.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:36.694
In addition to Abraham, Glenn, and Alpha,
there's Spencer, Simon, and Beta.

00:02:36.694 --> 00:02:41.108
One has to wonder if he has more records to
earn with his arc still unfinished.

00:02:41.108 --> 00:02:46.196
Jeffrey Dean Morgan is an excellent Negan,
and he's made the now-iconic role all his own.

00:02:46.196 --> 00:02:50.790
The image of him in his black leather jacket,
combat boots, slicked-back hair, flashing

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:55.028
a devious smile through his tight graying
beard is instantly recognizable.

00:02:55.028 --> 00:02:59.630
It's impossible to imagine anyone other than
Morgan taking on the part, but that was very

00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:00.634
nearly the case.

00:03:00.634 --> 00:03:05.380
When Walking Dead artist Charlie Adlard created
the look of the character, he based Negan

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:10.234
on musician Henry Rollins, who auditioned
for the Negan role before Morgan gave it a swing.

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:15.400
Rollins spoke to Forbes in 2016 and discussed
the process, recalling the excitement online

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.766
about Negan's Walking Dead debut, saying,

00:03:17.766 --> 00:03:22.060
"The internet was wild with speculation because,
in the upcoming season, they were going to

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:23.340
introduce the character.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.180
[...] I went for the audition, and there were
five pages of really cool dialogue with all

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.378
these curses and it was beautiful, but I didn't
get it."

00:03:30.378 --> 00:03:34.350
Rollins added that while many thought he should've
gotten the part, he was very impressed with

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:36.160
Jeffrey Dean Morgan's approach.

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:40.670
Rollins also wasn't the only big name who
vied for the Negan gig, as Scream's own Matthew

00:03:40.670 --> 00:03:42.670
Lillard gave it a shot as well.

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:48.935
Despite, or perhaps because of, his terrifying
nature, Negan became one of the show's most popular characters.

00:03:48.935 --> 00:03:54.774
So popular, in fact, that he's even managed
to cross over into unrelated video games on several occasions.

00:03:54.774 --> 00:03:59.830
Arguably the most well-known appearance was
his guest spot in the 2015 fighting game Tekken

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:05.380
7, complete with his own unique fighting style,
moves, and a stage based on his TV introduction.

00:04:05.380 --> 00:04:06.390
Need more Negan?

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:11.640
In December of 2019, both Negan and Michonne
were added to PlayerUnknown's Battlegrounds

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:13.180
Mobile for a limited time.

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:17.450
And if you're into Magic: The Gathering, Negan
was included as one of the new cards of the

00:04:17.450 --> 00:04:20.053
controversial Walking Dead expansion.

00:04:20.053 --> 00:04:24.780
For as beloved as Negan has become, it's worth
remembering that the character itself wasn't

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.000
conjured up out of thin air for television.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:33.878
Negan first arrived in The Walking Dead #100,
surviving to see the series finale in issue #193.

00:04:33.878 --> 00:04:38.870
Much like he does on the Walking Dead TV show,
the leader of the Saviors makes a grand entrance

00:04:38.870 --> 00:04:43.565
with Lucille in hand, spouting expletives
and putting all of his enemies on notice.

00:04:43.565 --> 00:04:48.700
As it turns out, Morgan took great care in
nailing Negan's brash yet collected personality.

00:04:49.258 --> 00:04:55.688
"You do realize the storm of ---- I'm gonna
dump on Rick soon as I am clear of the ----storm

00:04:55.688 --> 00:04:57.116
he dumped on me."

00:04:57.531 --> 00:05:03.310
In February of 2016, Jeffrey Dean Morgan spoke
to Entertainment Weekly and detailed why pushing

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:08.070
the strong language envelope was so important,
regardless of how AMC felt, saying,

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:13.540
"We're going to push AMC — the plan is to
push them as far as they can because it's who Negan is.

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:16.870
[...] Negan is a guy that you want to keep
as true as possible, and that would be how

00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:18.370
I want to play him as well."

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:23.030
Looking back on the cultural impact of Negan's
character, it's fair to say Morgan did just

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:24.511
that and then some.

